{"hits": {"hits": [{"created": "1978-07-01T00:00:00+00:00", "updated": "2023-03-07T01:18:51.653574+00:00", "links": {"bibtex": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/131122?format=bibtex", "latex-eu": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/131122?format=latex-eu", "latex-us": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/131122?format=latex-us", "json": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/131122?format=json", "json-expanded": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/131122?format=json-expanded", "cv": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/131122?format=cv", "citations": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?q=refersto%3Arecid%3A131122"}, "metadata": {"authors": [{"full_name": "Amati, D."}, {"full_name": "Petronzio, R."}, {"full_name": "Veneziano, G."}], "publication_info": [{"journal_volume": "146", "page_end": "49", "year": 1978, "page_start": "29", "journal_title": "Nucl.Phys.B"}], "texkeys": ["Amati:1978by"], "imprints": [{"date": "1978"}], "abstracts": [{"value": "Extending previous techniques we obtain at all orders the factorization of mass singularities for every hard QCD process. These appear in a universal factor that can be reabsorbed into the standard parton density. Thus suitable ratios of cross sections can be computed by a perturbative expansion in the running coupling constant. Moreover, at the leading log level we obtain, after explicit cancellation of infrared divergences, the scaling violation of the operator product expansion."}], "control_number": 131122, "dois": [{"value": "10.1016/0550-3213(78)90430-3"}], "titles": [{"title": "Relating Hard QCD Processes Through Universality of Mass Singularities. 2."}, {"title": "QUANTUM CHROMODYNAMICS"}], "author_count": 3, "document_type": ["article"]}, "id": "131122"}], "total": 1}, "links": {"self": "https://inspirehep.net/api/literature/?sort=mostcited&q=j%20Nucl.Phys.B%2C146%2C29&size=3&page=1&fields=control_number,titles.title,authors.full_name,author_count,publication_info,arxiv_eprints.value,dois.value,t